<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Operation Adelaide, 2016</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;This scenario assumes an armed conflict has&amp;nbsp;broken out&amp;nbsp;between Liberia and Sierra Leone.&amp;nbsp; Sierra Leone has crossed the border into Liberian territory and has occupied the town of Bo Waterside.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Sierra Leone has refused to withdraw from Bo&amp;nbsp;Waterside and&amp;nbsp;Liberia has requested help from the United States.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;-------------------------------------------------------&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;This scenario assumes that LCS 6 &lt;EM&gt;Jackson&lt;/EM&gt; has been fitted with a COIL laser weapon.&amp;nbsp; The mission bay on the &lt;EM&gt;Independence&lt;/EM&gt;-class littoral combat ships&amp;nbsp;has turned out to be an ideal platform for the&amp;nbsp;large power source needed for&amp;nbsp;a directed&amp;nbsp;energy weapon.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;Adelaide is, of course, a randomly selected code name and has nothing to do with the actual city of&amp;nbsp;Adelaide.&amp;nbsp; At least, that is what&amp;nbsp;they want you to think...&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;A delta template .ini file has been included in the .zip file to assist in updating the scenario to any future versions of the database.&amp;nbsp; &lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt"&gt;Scenario Author: Mark Gellis&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
